Rejected at STEP 0 after reading the full [paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/1906.02157).

The proposed family passes generation and verification but fails hardness:

- Track A: Theorems 3.1 and 3.4 explicitly construct the certificates.
- Track B: the compact and mechanical routes are identical.
- The next scalable KTS instance requires 351 answer atoms, exceeding G9(c)’s 256-atom cap.

The complete analysis, measured costs, theorem references, and surrogate-family rationale are in [REJECTED.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1906.02157/REJECTED.md). No generator or fabricated hardening artifacts were created.
